diff --git a/docs/deployment-configuration.md b/docs/deployment-configuration.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7fb8b1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment-configuration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+# Dashboard deployment configuration
+
+This candidate supports one host: collector, HTTP API and PostgreSQL bind to
+loopback, with a local reverse proxy serving the browser over HTTPS and node
+telemetry over WSS. The persistence client can use local WS or remote WSS.
+Backend settings are read at process startup. Invalid or missing settings stop
+startup before listening or opening the relevant database/WebSocket connection.
+
+The persistence, schema, runtime dependencies and complete browser path still
+need acceptance work. These settings are not a production launch approval.
+
+## Required settings
+
+| Process | Setting | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Collector | `COLLECTOR_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` or `::1` |
+| Collector | `COLLECTOR_PORT` | Explicit listener port |
+| Collector | `WS_CREDENTIALS_FILE` | Absolute private JSON file; see [enrollment](telemetry-enrollment.md) |
+| Persistence | `COLLECTOR_WS_URL` | Explicit URL ending in `/primus`; local WS or WSS |
+| API | `API_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` or `::1` |
+| API | `API_PORT` | Explicit listener port |
+| Persistence and API | `DB_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` or `::1` |
+| Persistence and API | `DB_PORT` | Database port, 1–65535 |
+| Persistence and API | `DB_NAME` | Provisioned database name |
+| Persistence and API | `DB_USER` | Provisioned role for this process |
+| Persistence and API | `DB_PASSWORD_FILE` | Absolute path to a private UTF-8 password file |
+| Browser build | `REACT_APP_STATS_API_PATH` | Same-origin API prefix, such as `/stats-api` |
+
+Listeners accept 0 for disposable ephemeral-port tests. Deployed services need
+fixed ports from 1–65535 so the proxy and persistence client can find them.
+There are no endpoint, database-name, user or password defaults. The old `PORT`
+does not configure either listener. `SQLHOST`/`SQLPASS` are rejected rather than
+silently retaining legacy database settings. `WS_SECRET` remains unsupported.
+
+The database password file contains one nonempty line, with an optional final
+LF or CRLF. Other whitespace belongs to the password and is preserved. Read
+errors do not include file paths or contents. Store this and the collector
+credential file outside the checkout; restrict access to the relevant service
+account and administrator. Do not put real secrets in examples or Git.
+
+Database transport is explicitly local plaintext (`ssl: false`). Remote database
+hosting and container port publication are outside this configuration. The
+existing five-connection pool limit is retained. Use separate database roles:
+the API reads only; persistence writes only its necessary tables. Database
+ownership, schema creation and migrations belong to a separate administrative
+role. Configuration validation cannot verify PostgreSQL grants or host access
+rules; those need an actual database acceptance test.
+
+`COLLECTOR_WS_URL` permits WS only to the numeric loopback addresses, or WSS to
+a configured host. Credentials in the URL, query strings, fragments and other
+paths are refused. Persistence consumes the viewer stream; it does not receive
+validator keys or use a node's telemetry credential.
+
+## Proxy and browser routing
+
+The proxy serves the compiled browser and forwards `/stats-api/` to the private
+API, removing that prefix. Thus `/stats-api/nodes` reaches backend `/nodes`.
+Configure `REACT_APP_STATS_API_PATH=/stats-api` when building the browser; it is
+public configuration compiled into the bundle. Changing it requires rebuilding.
+The validation executes when the browser module loads, not during the build.
+Only path segments containing letters, digits, underscores or hyphens are
+accepted; one final slash is normalized away. A missing or invalid value stops
+the UI rather than contacting an old foundation endpoint.
+
+The API no longer adds wildcard CORS headers. Browser/API hosting on unrelated
+origins is not supported by this candidate. CORS is not API authentication;
+public dashboard data remains public through the chosen proxy routes.
+
+Forward the collector's `/api` WebSocket path for efsn telemetry. Keep `/primus`
+local if only the same-host persistence process needs it. Do not expose the
+legacy `/external` stream automatically. The final proxy must provide certificates,
+WebSocket upgrade handling, suitable timeouts and bounded requests/connections.
+Those deployment settings and loss/reconnect behavior still need testing.
+
+For a local collector test after installing the locked dependencies:
+
+```sh
+NODE_ENV=production COLLECTOR_HOST=127.0.0.1 COLLECTOR_PORT=3000 WS_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/absolute/private/telemetry-credentials.json npm start
+```
+
+Use protected service environments to set each process's required values.
+No production domain, database or role is provisioned by this change.
+
+## Persistence blockers to resolve before integration
+
+Source review found the following inherited behavior. Configuration tests stub
+the storage layer and do not claim these paths work:
+
+- `wsclient/wsclient.js` starts cleanup/keepalive timers on every reconnect but
+  does not cancel them on close. The cleanup callback loses its interval value.
+- The same file shares initialization metadata and block/time fields across
+  nodes, reads `myData.data.id` without checking the envelope, and does not request
+  the initial viewer snapshot or handle Primus heartbeats explicitly.
+- Its startup call to `Populate.initDbAndTables()` deletes charts, then refers
+  to an undefined `record`; the caller does not await or catch that initialization.
+- `db_methods/populate.js` interpolates node report values into several SQL
+  statements. Use parameterized statements and verify ordinary quoted text
+  survives round trips before enabling persistence.
+- `POSTGRESQL_Setup.sh` starts by dropping a database, does not switch its
+  connection to the newly created database, and declares `utctime` as time of
+  day rather than a full timestamp. It also omits the API's `blocks` table.
+  Do not use this historical script as the new provisioning procedure.
+- API `/info` calls a missing retrieval method. API query bounds, error output,
+  stale-data labeling and actual frontend payload compatibility remain unverified.
+
+Resolve these with a small persistence correction and versioned, nondestructive
+schema setup, then test collector → storage → API → browser with distinct nodes,
+disconnect/reconnect, stale observations and dashboard loss. Complete runtime,
+dependency, TLS and resource-limit review before public use.
